<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Harry Johnston</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1858">1858</a>–<a href="/years/1927">1927</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Sir Harry Johnston</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sir Harry Johnston was a British explorer and colonial administrator. As vice-consul in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-delta">Niger Delta</a> he deported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaja-of-opobo">King Jaja</a> of Opobo in 1887. As commissioner of British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-africa">Central Africa</a> from 1891 he fought the Yao and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swahili">Swahili</a> chiefs around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-malawi">Lake Malawi</a>, founding Nyasaland, and as special commissioner in Uganda he negotiated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buganda-agreement">Buganda Agreement</a> of 1900.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/harry-johnston.jpg" alt="Harry Johnston" width="320" height="443" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Elliott &amp; Fry · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Harry_Johnston.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
